    "result": "{\"analysis\":\"All four proposals last round were refused only because the rationale gave a truncated KL value, so these resubmit the same directions with exact record values. Only iso_3.15 has been measured, and its bits are close to the budget, so a same-size upgrade needs a downgrade to fund it. No option setting has been measured, and the measured KL is above the single-layer-sum prediction, so interactions matter. Three proposals test GPTQ solver options at unchanged size. The fourth funds upgrades by coarsening rht_gptq_int3 groups. Its budget fit is an estimate, because the analysis does not list per-layer methods or sizes for all layers. Its upgrade KLs were measured with default options, so they may not carry over to the whole recipe.\",\"stop\":false,\"proposals\":[{\"name\":\"opt_act_order\",\"base\":\"iso_3.15\",\"changes\":[],\"options\":{\"gptq_int2\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true},\"gptq_int3\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true},\"gptq_int4\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true},\"rht_gptq_int2\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true},\"rht_gptq_int3\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true},\"rht_gptq_int4\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true}},\"rationale\":\"The base iso_3.15 measured KL 0.43614466651129274 [E514ab09c524e] and has no measured option variant. This grid keeps every layer method and sets act_order=true for all GPTQ-family methods, so stored bits do not change. It tests whether solver ordering lowers whole-recipe KL.\",\"cites\":[\"E514ab09c524e\"]},{\"name\":\"opt_damp_high\",\"base\":\"iso_3.15\",\"changes\":[],\"options\":{\"gptq_int2\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.1},\"gptq_int3\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.1},\"gptq_int4\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.1},\"rht_gptq_int2\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.1},\"rht_gptq_int3\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.1},\"rht_gptq_int4\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.1}},\"rationale\":\"The base iso_3.15 measured KL 0.43614466651129274 [E514ab09c524e] and has no measured damping variant. This grid keeps every layer method and sets damp=0.1 for all GPTQ-family methods, so stored bits do not change. It tests stronger regularization of the solver on the same calibration data.\",\"cites\":[\"E514ab09c524e\"]},{\"name\":\"opt_damp_low\",\"base\":\"iso_3.15\",\"changes\":[],\"options\":{\"gptq_int2\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.001},\"gptq_int3\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.001},\"gptq_int4\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.001},\"rht_gptq_int2\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.001},\"rht_gptq_int3\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.001},\"rht_gptq_int4\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.001}},\"rationale\":\"The base iso_3.15 measured KL 0.43614466651129274 [E514ab09c524e] and has no measured damping variant. This grid keeps every layer method and sets damp=0.001 for all GPTQ-family methods, so stored bits do not change. It tests the opposite damping direction from the higher-damping proposal.\",\"cites\":[\"E514ab09c524e\"]},{\"name\":\"g256_rht3_mlp_upgrades\",\"base\":\"iso_3.15\",\"changes\":[{\"block\":14,\"kind\":\"down_proj\",\"method\":\"rht_gptq_int3\"},{\"block\":2,\"kind\":\"up_proj\",\"method\":\"gptq_int4\"},{\"block\":3,\"kind\":\"up_proj\",\"method\":\"gptq_int4\"}],\"options\":{\"rht_gptq_int3\":{\"weight.group_size\":256}},\"rationale\":\"Setting group_size=256 on rht_gptq_int3 reduces its stored bits to pay for upgrades on layers where loss concentrates. Measured single-layer KL: model.layers.14.mlp.down_proj moves from rht_gptq_int2 0.00633466 [E4c3f9b73e065] to rht_gptq_int3 0.00181478 [E90bd4b2f3645]; model.layers.2.mlp.up_proj moves from gptq_int3 0.00641875 [E9baa10763ebe] to gptq_int4 0.00237045 [Ef3d9c7b4502c]; model.layers.3.mlp.up_proj moves from rht_gptq_int3 0.0064177 [E6f4f7ea296d5] to gptq_int4 0.00237732 [Ef4ee8cb4969e]. The KL cost of coarser groups has not been measured; this grid measures it against the base KL 0.43614466651129274 [E514ab09c524e].\",\"cites\":[\"E514ab09c524e\",\"E4c3f9b73e065\",\"E90bd4b2f3645\",\"E9baa10763ebe\",\"Ef3d9c7b4502c\",\"E6f4f7ea296d5\",\"Ef4ee8cb4969e\"]}]}",
